cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "spatial-edit-audit: controlled simulation and counterfactual audit toolkit for selective local spatial multi-omics edits"
abstract: "A deterministic, annotation-blind testbed for evaluating selective local editors on spatial multi-omics sections. Built on four public tissue sections (11,888 spots; 593 candidate tiles), it isolates channel-aggregation versus unilateral decoys, batch-quota coupling, single-pool split-conformal calibration, and static-reference circularity, and ships scripts that reproduce every frozen table from offline baselines."
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/swiftiejerry/spatial-edit-audit"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24389148"
keywords:
  - spatial multi-omics
  - selective prediction
  - benchmark methodology
  - conformal calibration
  - counterfactual audit
  - reproducibility
